Adapted from TheSimpsonsGameRecomp 6590289a (rex_audio_set_thread_priority, the Windows half): the audio worker, which runs the guest audio callbacks, and the XMA decoder thread run at THREAD_PRIORITY_TIME_CRITICAL, so they are not starved by the GPU and streaming threads under load (crunchy, slowed in-game audio there). Both threads block on their events when idle.

diff --git a/include/rex/audio/thread_priority.h b/include/rex/audio/thread_priority.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6ecd161
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/rex/audio/thread_priority.h
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+#pragma once
+
+namespace rex::audio {
+
+// Raises the calling audio thread to time-critical priority, so guest audio callbacks and XMA
+// decoding are not starved by the GPU and streaming threads under load.
+bool RaiseAudioThreadPriority();
+
+}  // namespace rex::audio
